<div id="A1.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The conventions for implementing the empirical CDF functions follow in the expected ways, but we briefly highlight the key considerations below, as they can impact the behavior of the estimators. An implementation in NumPy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite>, version 1.26.4, appears in Listing <a href="#LST4" title="Listing 4 ‣ A.5 Empirical CDF Function ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The distance quantiles should be exclusionary at the boundaries. When <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dNearest=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>nearest</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dNearest=0</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-{\rm{eCDF}}^{\cdot}_{\rm{ca}}(\dNearest)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>eCDF</mi><mi>ca</mi><mo>⋅</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>nearest</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-{\rm{eCDF}}^{\cdot}_{\rm{ca}}(\dNearest)</annotation></semantics></math> quantile should be 1, and when <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dNearest" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>nearest</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dNearest</annotation></semantics></math> is greater than the maximum observed distance (across <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\calibrationSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ca</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\calibrationSplit</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\testSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>te</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\testSplit</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\calibrationSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>ca</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\calibrationSplit</annotation></semantics></math>, and across <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\trainSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\trainSplit</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}\in\trainSplit" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>tr</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}\in\trainSplit</annotation></semantics></math>, the latter case only occurring during training), the <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-{\rm{eCDF}}^{\cdot}_{\rm{ca}}(\dNearest)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>eCDF</mi><mi>ca</mi><mo>⋅</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>nearest</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-{\rm{eCDF}}^{\cdot}_{\rm{ca}}(\dNearest)</annotation></semantics></math> quantile should be 0.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the quantiles over an <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sdm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">sdm</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sdm</annotation></semantics></math> activation, as needed for calibration, saturated values at the high-end should be assigned a quantile of 1. In the example code, this is achieved by setting the argument <span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">val_in_0to1=True</span>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.6 </span>Example Implementation of the Negative+Positive Vocabulary Normalization and <math id="A1.SS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> Regularization Term</h3>

<div id="A1.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The positive+negative vocabulary normalization and regularization loss (Eq. <a href="#S4.E32" title='In "sdm" Network Next-token Loss. ‣ 4.3.3 "sdm" network ‣ 4.3 From sdm Calibration to sdm Networks ‣ 4 Methods ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) are conceptually parsimonious and straightforward to implement. Code scaffolding for an example implementation of an <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sdm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">sdm</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sdm</annotation></semantics></math> network training loop appears in Listing <a href="#LST5" title="Listing 5 ‣ A.6 Example Implementation of the Negative+Positive Vocabulary Normalization and 𝐿^2 Regularization Term ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Similarity-Distance-Magnitude Universal Verification" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. For computational expediency, here (as in the experiments in the main text), the <math id="A1.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\q</annotation></semantics></math> values and distance quantiles are calculated after each epoch, although in principle, they can be calculated with updated network values as an epoch progresses.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST5" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:345.0pt;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 5: </span>Code scaffolding in PyTorch, version 2.3.0, for a basic training loop of an <math id="LST5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sdm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">sdm</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sdm</annotation></semantics></math> network with the Negative+Positive Vocabulary Normalization and <math id="LST5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> regularization term, where the <math id="LST5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\q</annotation></semantics></math> values and distance quantiles are updated after each epoch.</figcaption>
<div id="LST5.2" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx92" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx92.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">pdist</span><span id="lstnumberx92.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx92.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx92.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx92.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">nn</span><span id="lstnumberx92.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span><span id="lstnumberx92.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">PairwiseDistance</span><span id="lstnumberx92.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx92.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">p</span><span id="lstnumberx92.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=2)</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx93" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx93.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">criterion</span><span id="lstnumberx93.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx93.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx93.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx93.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">nn</span><span id="lstnumberx93.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">.</span><span id="lstnumberx93.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">NLLLoss</span><span id="lstnumberx93.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">()</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx94" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx94.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">for</span><span id="lstnumberx94.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx94.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">e</span><span id="lstnumberx94.4" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx94.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">in</span><span id="lstnumberx94.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx94.7" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">range</span><span id="lstnumberx94.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx94.9" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">total_epochs</span><span id="lstnumberx94.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">):</span>
</div>
<div id="lstnumberx95" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="lstnumberx95.1" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter">    </span><span id="lstnumberx95.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">total_mini_batches</span><span id="lstnumberx95.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx95.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">=</span><span id="lstnumberx95.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx95.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">len</span><span id="lstnumberx95.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(</span><span id="lstnumberx95.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">range</span><span id="lstnumberx95.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">(0,</span><span id="lstnumberx95.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx95.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">train_size</span><span id="lstnumberx95.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">,</span><span id="lstnumberx95.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter"> </span><span id="lstnumberx95.14" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter">batch_size</span><span id="lstnumberx95.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">))</span>
</div>
